{
  "id": "xsd-catalog",
  "area": "xsd",
  "description": "XSD validation with the W3C test-suite catalog schemas, standing in for UBL 2.1 (no UBL XSDs exist under testdata/: the Peppol and XRechnung inputs ship rules, stylesheets and instances only). Schemas: the XSLT 3.0 test-catalog schema (admin/catalog-schema.xsd, 144 KB, XSD 1.0 with vc: version attributes, local xml.xsd import) and the QT3 catalog schema (78 KB). Instances: real test-set catalogs from 3.6 KB to 2.5 MB. Invalid items are a QT3 test set given to the XSLT schema and an XSLT test set given to the QT3 schema (other namespace), and the XSLT suite's _base-expressions.xml: all three fail at the root (cvc-elt.1), not deep in the content. go-xml validates as XSD 1.0 so xmllint is comparable; Xerces always runs its 1.1 processor.",
  "inputs": "testdata/xslt30-test/, testdata/qt3tests/",
  "normalise": "none",
  "xsd_version": "1.0",
  "engines": ["go-xml", "xmllint", "xerces-j-xsd11"],
  "modes": ["cold", "warm"],
